    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASAN output confirms a heap-buffer-overflow READ at `value_move` (`src/value_array.h:20`) called from `mrb_ary_splice` (`src/array.c:804`), exactly matching our analysis.\n\nThe 19-byte Ruby script `a=[1]\\na[0,5]=[2,3]` causes the crash because `mrb_ary_splice` computes `tail = head + len` before clamping `len` to the actual array length, but never updates `tail`. The stale `tail` value makes `alen - tail` negative, which wraps to a huge `size_t` when passed to `value_move`, reading past the heap buffer.",
